es are now lying in the mississippi  river and they're not usable so crews  are having to find  power outside of this region and bring  it here on new long transmission lines  they close down the main highway into  new orleans today to string a new line  across the interstate so they can get  power here  dave uh since hurricane katrina 16 years  ago much of the infrastructure has been  improved in the region to withstand  these storms but with climate change  they are becoming more frequent what  more needs to be done long term  well they want here in new orleans the  worst of the damage was spared the  levees held this time for ida unlike  they did against hurricane katrina many  people since katrina have been saying  due to climate change and sea surface  levels rising we need better protections  against hurricanes this seems to be  proof that these new hardened taller  stronger levees around new orleans have  prevented 80 percent of the city being  flooded this time like there were in  katrina now  in  in areas outside of new orleans leaders  are begging for similar kinds of  protection fearing that we're going to  see more and more of these monster  storms moving forward  thanks dave reporter dave cohen in new  orleans  you
 

